[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Crusader Kings II + Gyro: tilting the controller moves the cursor too, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}. Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller.
The right stick {rs} moves the pointer: {rt} or {south} is a left click, {lt} a right click (move an army, or open a province holder's character). The left stick {ls} pans the map.
{north} pauses and unpauses; the {leftright} d-pad slows the game down and speeds it up, and {updown} zooms.
Hold {west} for Shift while you click: add an army to the selection, add a waypoint, or open the top liege of a province.
Hold {lb} for the map modes and {rb} for the army orders, aimed with the right stick {rs}: release to pick.
{select} lists the screens, the ledger and the finders (tap it, pick with {south}, {east} closes the list). {east} or {start} is Escape: it closes the open window, and on the map opens the game menu.
Click {l3} for your character, and hold it to go back to your capital. Click {r3} for the character finder.
Hold {guide} and press {west} for the on-screen keyboard (save names, searches).
The keys are the game's defaults from the Paradox wiki's hotkey list, not checked on an install, and Crusader Kings II can't rebind them. Its speed keys are + and -, sent here from the numpad. It has no controller support and no quick save: save from the game menu.'''

